Go ahead. Try to lift it.

362
00:29:18,523 --> 00:29:20,685
- I can't.
- Good.

363
00:29:20,859 --> 00:29:22,384
Then we'll go back in time.

364
00:29:22,561 --> 00:29:25,395
The year is 1936.

365
00:29:25,564 --> 00:29:27,726
Do you remember 1936?

366
00:29:29,735 --> 00:29:32,637
Yeah. RUTH: What is your name?

367
00:29:34,306 --> 00:29:37,606
Emily. Emily Long.

368
00:29:37,776 --> 00:29:42,305
- And how old are you, Emily?
- Seven and a half.

369
00:29:43,015 --> 00:29:44,608
Where do you live?

370
00:29:44,783 --> 00:29:47,719
On a big cotton
farm outside Athens.

371
00:29:47,886 --> 00:29:49,354
Emily,

372
00:29:50,022 --> 00:29:52,617
would you write your name
and age on this, please?

373
00:30:16,615 --> 00:30:21,246
Emily, do you remember
a terrible day in 1936

374
00:30:21,420 --> 00:30:24,549
when something came
crashing out of the sky?

375
00:30:24,723 --> 00:30:27,989
- Yeah.
- Could you tell me about it?

376
00:30:30,095 --> 00:30:32,496
- Do I have to?
- Don't be afraid.

377
00:30:32,664 --> 00:30:34,530
Nothing's gonna happen.

378
00:30:35,200 --> 00:30:37,635
You went out in the
fields that day, didn't you?

379
00:30:39,604 --> 00:30:42,870
My daddy was picking cotton
and I went out to help him.

380
00:30:43,041 --> 00:30:46,011
We always had a really
good time picking cotton.

381
00:30:46,578 --> 00:30:48,376
Then what happened?

382
00:30:50,015 --> 00:30:53,383
- There was a noise.
- What kind of a noise?

383
00:30:55,987 --> 00:30:58,218
It was like a scream.

384
00:31:00,058 --> 00:31:03,256
And it got louder and louder.

385
00:31:03,862 --> 00:31:09,392
And then I seen a big, shiny
bird diving to the ground.

386
00:31:09,935 --> 00:31:12,200
I got scared and I cried.

387
00:31:12,904 --> 00:31:15,999
Mommy. Mommy.

388
00:31:18,143 --> 00:31:23,707
And then... And then the
bird crashed into the ground

389
00:31:24,549 --> 00:31:28,543
and broke into all these pieces
and there was fire everywhere.

390
00:31:30,555 --> 00:31:35,619
And my daddy tried to get close
but he couldn't. It was too hot.

391
00:31:35,794 --> 00:31:38,593
Did you go back out
after the fire was out?

392
00:31:38,764 --> 00:31:42,030
Yeah, once everything
was burned up.

393
00:31:42,734 --> 00:31:45,863
Daddy said it was an airplane.

394
00:31:48,573 --> 00:31:52,374
We even found pieces of
the tail and hid it in a creek

395
00:31:52,544 --> 00:31:56,481
opposite the big
old diving tree.

396
00:31:56,648 --> 00:31:58,549
Why'd you hide it, Emily?

397
00:31:58,717 --> 00:32:03,519
Daddy said the crash was our secret.
He didn't want anybody else to know.

398
00:32:05,490 --> 00:32:07,891
We hid something else too.

399
00:32:08,727 --> 00:32:10,218
What else did you hide?

400
00:32:11,530 --> 00:32:13,829
Big piece of metal.

401
00:32:14,433 --> 00:32:17,335
Daddy said it was
part of the engine.

402
00:32:17,936 --> 00:32:20,599
And we buried it
by grandpa's grave.

403
00:32:20,772 --> 00:32:24,265
Emily, why did your daddy
say that you couldn't tell anyone?

404
00:32:25,477 --> 00:32:27,446
I don't know.

405
00:32:27,612 --> 00:32:31,640
Emily, you told me before.
I want you to tell me again.

406
00:32:35,086 --> 00:32:41,151
I think... I think Daddy took
something out of the airplane.

407
00:32:51,169 --> 00:32:53,195
I have never seen
anything like that before.

408
00:32:53,371 --> 00:32:55,169
Something remarkable
just happened in there.

409
00:32:55,340 --> 00:32:57,605
She's never mentioned
the engine part before.

410
00:32:57,776 --> 00:33:01,679
Don't you see? If I can find the
piece, that means my research is true.

411
00:33:01,847 --> 00:33:04,783
- Feel free to go inside.
- Thanks.

412
00:33:09,387 --> 00:33:11,219
Hi, Pat. PAT: Heh.

413
00:33:11,389 --> 00:33:12,982
Hi.

414
00:33:14,092 --> 00:33:16,186
So how are you doing?

415
00:33:16,361 --> 00:33:18,057
Fine, heh.

416
00:33:19,130 --> 00:33:21,690
- Do you remember anything?
- No.

417
00:33:21,867 --> 00:33:23,495
You know, it's strange though,

418
00:33:23,668 --> 00:33:27,696
