489
00:39:09,347 --> 00:39:13,512
She sings with the choir
at church where I work.

490
00:39:14,185 --> 00:39:16,086
I'm a custodial engineer.

491
00:39:16,254 --> 00:39:17,882
Do you see her very often?

492
00:39:18,056 --> 00:39:20,685
They rehearse a couple of
times a week, so I see her then.

493
00:39:20,859 --> 00:39:24,091
And on Sundays. She's
always there on Sundays.

494
00:39:24,262 --> 00:39:26,561
Do you ever go to her house?

495
00:39:26,731 --> 00:39:30,224
She invited me over to help
decorate her Christmas tree last year.

496
00:39:30,401 --> 00:39:32,563
It was just her and me.

497
00:39:34,138 --> 00:39:36,039
So how do you feel about her?

498
00:39:39,310 --> 00:39:40,403
I like her.

499
00:39:40,578 --> 00:39:44,674
- A lot?
- Yeah. Uh, she's my friend.

500
00:39:44,849 --> 00:39:46,889
Your Honor, I fail to see
the relevance of all this.

501
00:39:47,018 --> 00:39:49,647
Uh, Your Honor, I know
this seems far afield,

502
00:39:49,821 --> 00:39:54,521
but, uh, I give you my word, it's
not only relevant, it's essential.

503
00:39:54,692 --> 00:39:56,126
Proceed.

504
00:39:57,262 --> 00:39:59,697
Uh, Mickey,

505
00:39:59,864 --> 00:40:03,733
uh, I can't help
but notice that, uh,

506
00:40:03,902 --> 00:40:07,930
you hang around Miss Emerson
a lot when she's in church.

507
00:40:08,106 --> 00:40:11,167
- Don't you?
- Uh-huh. Sometimes.

508
00:40:11,342 --> 00:40:14,870
- How come?
- I don't know.

509
00:40:15,046 --> 00:40:18,448
I like her. I like to watch her.

510
00:40:19,017 --> 00:40:21,612
I wanna make sure she's okay.

511
00:40:22,086 --> 00:40:29,653
You know, a lot of people
might call a feeling like that love.

